================================================================================
Bundled sidecar executables
================================================================================

These ship as separate executables. They are invoked as subprocesses and are
never linked into the application binary. Each is accompanied, in the released
bundle, by its licence text, the build configuration actually used, and a
written offer of corresponding source on the same distribution channel.

mpv
  Licence: GPL-2.0-or-later
  Role:    playback engine, out of process (docs/adr/0013)
  Version: pinned per OS at release time; the pinned version, checksum, and
           build configuration land here with the first bundling task (E0-16).

ffmpeg, ffprobe
  Licence: LGPL-2.1-or-later, built without --enable-gpl, --enable-nonfree,
           and --enable-version3
  Role:    probe and on-demand component pack (docs/adr/0014)
  Version: pinned per OS at release time; recorded here with the first
           bundling task (E0-16).

Full redistribution obligations are enumerated in docs/DEPENDENCIES.md §5.

================================================================================
Statically linked Rust crates and npm packages
================================================================================

The complete, generated attribution list for the crates and npm packages we
redistribute — with each licence text, and the upstream NOTICE files that
Apache-2.0 requires — is produced at build time by `xtask check-notices` and
shipped inside the bundle. It is generated rather than hand-maintained so it
cannot drift from the lockfiles.

Obligations already known to need special handling, per docs/DEPENDENCIES.md §6:

  encoding_rs       BSD-3-Clause notice, including the no-endorsement clause
  moka              attribution under both licence parts
  walkdir           Unlicense OR MIT
  notify            CC0-1.0
  lucide-react      ISC, attribution required

No MPL-2.0, GPL, or LGPL code is statically linked into this application.
